n, Ron Day, John Newnham, John Hall.","Congratulations to Richard Dorman and Stephen Marshall on gaining British Vests during the year. Regretably Stephen has had his year torn apart due to work commitments.","1.C.Maddocks (Dawlish) 41.45; 3.G.Seatter 42.26; 4.C.Lawton 43.37; 6.S. Marshall 44.56; 9.R.Tanner 46.00; Team: 1.BELGRAVE 13; 2.Dawlish 21; 3.Splott Conservatives 22.","Coming up through in the longer events and behind Stephen Marshall in the Barking was Michael Feighan breaking the cadets course record, he also had the audacity to finish 3rd Belgrave man in the club 20m run.","Results; 1.I.McCombie (C.H.) 85.34; 2.C.Maddocks (Dawlish) 86.51; 3.T.Berrett (Tonbridge) 90.18; 4.R.Dorman 91.32; 7.G.Seatter 93.24; 15.S.Marshall 96.55; 34.J.Hall 101.03; 38.J.Llewellyn 101.28; 56.J.Newnham 104.08; 118.J.Keown 128.12.","Results; S.Marshall 4:50.11; 22.R.Day 6:06.42; In the Cadets race held at the same time, M.Feighan won with a new record of approximately 5hr.35.","And there is Stephen Marshall too, who, having had his work commitments reduced should be back in the spotlight. John Hall has had to lie low for a while due to varicose vein problems but is now back on the road.","1.J.Hall 13.18; 2.S.Marshall 13.37; 3.C.Lawton 13.59; 4.R.Tanner 14.01; 5.N.Foster 14.12; 6.J.Newnham 14.21; 7.M.Feighan 14.51; 8.S.Till (SWC) 14.57; 9.D.Fotheringham 15.11; 10.J.Bromley 16.17; 13.D.Sharpe 19.22;"]}